The issue was a `NotImplementedError: Unknown calibration type` in `satpy/readers/core/seviri.py` when `cal_type` was neither 1 nor 2. Based on the provided context, files produced after 2008-11-30 contain unsupported values for `PlannedChanProcessing` (which becomes `cal_type`), but these should still be handled by the effective radiance calibration logic (`_erads2bt`).

I have modified `ir_calibrate` in `satpy/readers/core/seviri.py` to default to `_erads2bt` if `cal_type` is not 1, removing the `NotImplementedError`.

```python
    def ir_calibrate(self, data, channel_name, cal_type):
        """Calibrate to brightness temperature."""
        if cal_type == 1:
            # spectral radiances
            return self._srads2bt(data, channel_name)
        # effective radiances
        return self._erads2bt(data, channel_name)
```

